."}, {"full_name": "Specka, A."}, {"full_name": "Steder, M."}, {"full_name": "Stella, B."}, {"full_name": "Stiewe, J."}, {"full_name": "Stoilov, A."}, {"full_name": "Straumann, U."}, {"full_name": "Sunar, D."}, {"full_name": "Tchoulakov, V."}, {"full_name": "Thompson, G."}, {"full_name": "Thompson, P.D."}, {"full_name": "Toll, T."}, {"full_name": "Tomasz, F."}, {"full_name": "Traynor, D."}, {"full_name": "Trinh, T.N."}, {"full_name": "Truol, P."}, {"full_name": "Tsakov, I."}, {"full_name": "Tsipolitis, G."}, {"full_name": "Tsurin, I."}, {"full_name": "Turnau, J."}, {"full_name": "Tzamariudaki, E."}, {"full_name": "Urban, K."}, {"full_name": "Urban, M."}, {"full_name": "Usik, A."}, {"full_name": "Utkin, D."}, {"full_name": "Valkarova, A."}, {"full_name": "Vallee, C."}, {"full_name": "Van Mechelen, P."}, {"full_name": "Vargas Trevino, A."}, {"full_name": "Vazdik, Y."}, {"full_name": "Veelken, C."}, {"full_name": "Vinokurova, S."}, {"full_name": "Volchinski, V."}, {"full_name": "Wacker, K."}, {"full_name": "Weber, G."}, {"full_name": "Weber, R."}, {"full_name": "Wegener, D."}, {"full_name": "Werner, C."}, {"full_name": "Wessels, M."}, {"full_name": "Wessling, B."}, {"full_name": "Wissing, C."}, {"full_name": "Wolf, R."}, {"full_name": "Wunsch, E."}, {"full_name": "Xella, S."}, {"full_name": "Yan, W."}, {"full_name": "Yeganov, V."}, {"full_name": "Zacek, J."}, {"full_name": "Zalesak, J."}, {"full_name": "Zhang, Z."}, {"full_name": "Zhelezov, A."}, {"full_name": "Zhokin, A."}, {"full_name": "Zhu, Y.C."}, {"full_name": "Zimmermann, J."}, {"full_name": "Zimmermann, T."}, {"full_name": "Zohrabyan, H."}, {"full_name": "Zomer, F."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "48", "page_end": "748", "year": 2006, "page_start": "715", "journal_title": "Eur.Phys.J.C"}], "texkeys": ["H1:2006zyl", "Aktas:2006hy"], "collaborations": [{"value": "H1"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "A detailed analysis is presented of the diffractive deep-inelastic scattering process $ep\\to eXY$, where $Y$ is a proton or a low mass proton excitation carrying a fraction $1 - \\xpom > 0.95$ of the incident proton longitudinal momentum and the squared four-momentum transfer at the proton vertex satisfies $|t|&lt;1 {\\rm GeV^2}$. Using data taken by the H1 experiment, the cross section is measured for photon virtualities in the range $3.5 \\leq Q^2 \\leq 1600 \\rm GeV^2$, triple differentially in $\\xpom$, $Q^2$ and $\\beta = x / \\xpom$, where $x$ is the Bjorken scaling variable. At low $\\xpom$, the data are consistent with a factorisable $\\xpom$ dependence, which can be described by the exchange of an effective pomeron trajectory with intercept $\\alphapom(0)= 1.118 \\pm 0.008 {\\rm (exp.)} ^{+0.029}_{-0.010} {\\rm (model)}$. Diffractive parton distribution functions and their uncertainties are determined from a next-to-leading order DGLAP QCD analysis of the $Q^2$ and $\\beta$ dependences of the cross section. The resulting gluon distribution carries an integrated fraction of around 70% of the exchanged momentum in the $Q^2$ range studied. Total and differential cross sections are also measured for the diffractive charged current process $e^+ p \\to \\bar{\\nu}_e XY$ and are found to be well described by predictions based on the diffractive parton distributions. The ratio of the diffractive to the inclusive neutral current $ep$ cross sections is studied. Over most of the kinematic range, this ratio shows no significant dependence on $Q^2$ at fixed $\\xpom$ and $x$ or on $x$ at fixed $Q^2$ and $\\beta$."}], "titles": [{"title": "Measurement and QCD analysis of the diffractive deep-inelastic scattering cross-section at HERA"}, {"title": "QUANTUM CHROMODYNAMICS"}, {"title": "DEEP INELASTIC"}, {"title": "CROSS-SECTION"}, {"title": "Measurement and QCD analysis of the diffractive deep-inelastic scattering cross-section at HERA"}, {"title": "Measurement and QCD Analysis of the Diffractive Deep-Inelastic Scattering Cross Section at HERA"}], "author_count": 294, "control_n